525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The financial feasibility of the project is therefore highly contingent on strict cost control in both capital expenditure and operating expense categories. Without effective procurement strategies and streamlined overhead structures, the risk of value erosion becomes considerable. These results strongly suggest the necessity of proactive risk mitigation: contractual locking of unit prices, performance-based management compensation structures, and lean operational frameworks. Additionally, sensitivity boundaries identified in this analysis should guide the construction of contingency budgets and be reflected in stakeholder risk communications. In summary, the two-way sensitivity analysis underscores a narrow feasibility window, where the project remains viable only if disciplined cost containment is achieved across both parameters.)
/E (The financial feasibility of the project is therefore highly contingent on strict cost control in both capital expenditure and operating expense categories. Without effective procurement strategies and streamlined overhead structures, the risk of value erosion becomes considerable. These results strongly suggest the necessity of proactive risk mitigation: contractual locking of unit prices, performance-based management compensation structures, and lean operational frameworks. Additionally, sensitivity boundaries identified in this analysis should guide the construction of contingency budgets and be reflected in stakeholder risk communications. In summary, the two-way sensitivity analysis underscores a narrow feasibility window, where the project remains viable only if disciplined cost containment is achieved across both parameters.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (To further understand how each input variable influenced output variability, sensitivity analysis was conducted using tornado and spider charts. The tornado chart revealed that the kitchen rental price was the dominant risk driver, accounting for 71.12% of the total explained variation in NPV_TIPV. The general price for all kitchen types added further variance, and when combined, these two inputs explained over 94% of the output variation. The occupancy rate in year 0 played a smaller yet still relevant role in overall sensitivity. These findings highlight that pricing strategies, particularly for standard large kitchens, should be actively managed as a key lever of financial performance.)
/E (To further understand how each input variable influenced output variability, sensitivity analysis was conducted using tornado and spider charts. The tornado chart revealed that the kitchen rental price was the dominant risk driver, accounting for 71.12% of the total explained variation in NPV_TIPV. The general price for all kitchen types added further variance, and when combined, these two inputs explained over 94% of the output variation. The occupancy rate in year 0 played a smaller yet still relevant role in overall sensitivity. These findings highlight that pricing strategies, particularly for standard large kitchens, should be actively managed as a key lever of financial performance.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
