565 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Environmental management is a critical component of the Shared Kitchen 4.0 infrastructure, particularly given the F&B sector's traditionally high environmental footprint. The project addresses this by integrating waste mitigation and environmental control systems within the building design. A centralized greywater treatment facility is installed at each kitchen cluster, which filters and treats effluents before discharging them into the municipal sewer system, thus complying with TCVN 14:2008 standards on industrial wastewater treatment. The treated water meets Category B standards \(non-potable reuse\), which can be recycled for non-consumptive purposes like sanitation and landscaping.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2]
